{
  "paragraphs": [
    "basket_labels: 111 of 119 rows have known values (93.3% coverage).",
    "At k = 20, mean shared-label agreement is 84.7% when weighting positive anchor\u2013label pairs, and 83.1% when weighting labels equally. Mean individual label lift is 2.249 and equal-label lift is 2.683. Mean lift is not aggregate purity divided by aggregate chance.",
    "daily: 69 known positives; 69 evaluable positive anchors have 87.8% mean agreement, versus 62.2% reference prevalence (lift 1.412). An average of 18.77 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "gift: 27 known positives; 27 evaluable positive anchors have 80.7% mean agreement, versus 24.3% reference prevalence (lift 3.319). An average of 18.07 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "seasonal: 27 known positives; 27 evaluable positive anchors have 80.7% mean agreement, versus 24.3% reference prevalence (lift 3.319). An average of 18.07 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "Known-neighbor coverage at this k is 92.7%. Unknown neighbors are excluded from agreement denominators; missing annotations can bias the result.",
    "The saved null comparison gives an empirical one-sided p-value of 0.25 for macro_lift. This tests the specified shuffle, not semantic understanding; use the combined multiple-testing table and practical effect sizes when judging the finding.",
    "The probe panel measures recoverability on a held-out split. Compare each model with its baseline; recoverability and nearest-neighbor usefulness answer different questions.",
    "baseline: balanced_accuracy 0.5, macro_f1 0.3907; 27 held-out test rows (or the macro summary of supported binary tags).",
    "linear: balanced_accuracy 0.9697, macro_f1 0.9735; 27 held-out test rows (or the macro summary of supported binary tags).",
    "Embedding A normalization comparison on identical held-out rows: raw_standardized: balanced_accuracy 0.9697, unit: balanced_accuracy 0.9697, unit_standardized: balanced_accuracy 0.9697, norm_only: balanced_accuracy 0.445. Direction-only and magnitude-only scores describe accessible information for these pipelines; fit telemetry does not establish encoder-training stability.",
    "In the raw_euclidean filtration for embedding A, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 2 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "In the unit_chordal filtration for embedding A, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 2 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "Next: compare feature measurements across scales, check probe gains against baselines, or summarize a selected region. Shared labels and correlated features can suggest patterns, but do not establish why the model retrieved an item."
